    "title": "<p><strong>Box&nbsp;9.02</strong> Differential diagnosis of intraductal papillary neoplasm of the bile ducts</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Yasuni Nakanuma",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 386.55pt; border: solid #BFBFBF 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"515\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Micropapillary biliary intraepithelial neoplasia (BilIN)</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Microscopically recognizable lesions in the intrahepatic large bile ducts</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; &lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;mm in height</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Constantly intermixed with flat or pseudopapillary BilIN</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Intraductal tubulopapillary neoplasm</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Cast-like lesion composed of densely packed neoplastic tubular glands in the duct</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Unequivocal architectural and cytological atypia (high grade)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; No mucinous content, negative for MUC5AC</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Intraductal polypoid metastasis from extrahepatic organs</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Metastasis from colorectal carcinoma is common</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
